1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,290
This is CardioLens.

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:10,750
Routine clinical data goes in, and a 3D
heart shows where coronary risk is likely

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,590
to be, artery by artery.

4
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:19,650
Cardiovascular disease remains a leading
cause of death worldwide,

5
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,830
and a narrowed coronary artery is usually
confirmed by angiography,

6
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,330
an invasive test.

7
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:28,670
Track A asks a different question: can
routine data,

8
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,390
such as age, blood pressure, an ECG and a
few lab values,

9
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:36,250
predict coronary artery disease and the
narrowing of each main artery,

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,190
and show it on an interactive 3D model?

11
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:42,630
Here is every requirement, and where
CardioLens meets it.

12
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,750
We used the extension of the Z-Alizadeh
Sani dataset from UCI:

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,150
303 patients, 55 features, and four
targets: CAD,

14
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,290
plus the LAD, LCX and RCA arteries.

15
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:58,110
No values were missing, and a constant
column was dropped.

16
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,550
The label columns are never model inputs.

17
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,010
That's asserted before every fit, and the
API rejects them:

18
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:05,290
requirement 1d.

19
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:10,010
We add clinical features, such as a
pretest probability,

20
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,010
kidney function and lipid ratios.

21
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:15,210
Twenty percent of patients are held out
until the very end.

22
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:18,890
The rest go through five-by-five
cross-validation with nested tuning,

23
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:23,140
and confidence intervals come from a
thousand bootstrap resamples.

24
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:27,590
Nine model families were compared for
every target,

25
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:31,430
from logistic regression to boosting and
stacked ensembles.

26
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:36,310
For the arteries, independent models did
as well as chained or hierarchical ones,

27
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,970
so we kept the simplest.

28
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,590
Every model is calibrated, so eighty
percent means about eight in ten,

29
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,410
with tuned thresholds and three risk
tiers.

30
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:49,130
On the untouched hold-out set, the ROC-AUC
is 0.895 for CAD,

31
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:55,010
0.832 for LAD, 0.768 for LCX and 0.741 for
RCA, with confidence intervals and every

32
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,690
metric from requirement 1e.

33
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:59,230
Each estimate is explained with exact SHAP
values,

34
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:03,470
mapped back to the raw measurements, in
about 150 milliseconds.

35
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,230
How does a probability become a picture?

36
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:12,130
One anatomy map holds every mesh name,
colour and label,

37
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:16,370
and a pure function turns each prediction
into a render-ready scene.

38
00:02:16,495 --> 00:02:20,590
Colour shows probability, on one shared
scale that is safe for colour-blind

39
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:24,210
viewers. Crossing a threshold adds an
outline and a pulse,

40
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:27,510
and every estimate carries a reliability
badge.

41
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:32,420
The data says whether an artery is
narrowed, but not where.

42
00:02:32,510 --> 00:02:36,660
So whole arteries are coloured, and
unlabelled branches stay neutral.

43
00:02:37,610 --> 00:02:40,960
Optional overlays show perfusion
territories, and the body regions behind

44
00:02:41,010 --> 00:02:43,980
each risk factor, never the disease
itself.

45
00:02:44,150 --> 00:02:47,600
And what-if shows associations, not
treatment effects.

46
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:51,380
Building the heart.

47
00:02:51,430 --> 00:02:55,440
Our first version was a procedural heart,
which is still kept as a fallback.

48
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:59,680
For realism, we moved to the Realistic
Human Heart by neshallads on Sketchfab,

49
00:02:59,730 --> 00:03:01,825
under CC BY 4.0.

50
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:05,760
A headless Blender script aligns it,
scales it to twelve centimetres,

51
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,020
and splits it into parts.

52
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:13,900
Its coronaries were only painted on, so we
traced them along the grooves,

53
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:16,640
smoothed them, and swept them into real
tubes.

54
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:19,740
One file carries a realistic and a
clinical look,

55
00:03:19,790 --> 00:03:22,440
plus invisible picking shapes and outline
shells.

56
00:03:22,490 --> 00:03:27,000
It's compressed to about 1.6 megabytes,
with a lighter version for phones,

57
00:03:27,050 --> 00:03:30,000
and a validator checks every name and
budget.

58
00:03:33,550 --> 00:03:34,750
Now, the app itself.

59
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:39,480
On a first visit it opens with a short
intro, then a three-step tour of where to

60
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:43,360
start, which you can skip, and it's
remembered after that.

61
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:50,020
Sample patients are one click away: six
real hold-out patients,

62
00:03:50,070 --> 00:03:53,920
from clearly low risk to a deliberate
uncertainty example.

63
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:56,100
Each one also has its own link.

64
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:01,900
You can also enter your own patient.

65
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:05,100
The form is generated from the API schema:
grouped,

66
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:08,000
searchable, and showing how many fields
changed.

67
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:12,860
Each field has a typical range, a help
note, and an effect meter showing how much

68
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:14,540
it can move the estimates.

69
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:18,900
Alt-click resets a single field, and a
full reset can be undone.

70
00:04:22,150 --> 00:04:24,470
Every change updates the estimate live.

71
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:28,300
Switch hypertension off, and a toast
reports exactly what moved:

72
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,280
CAD down 21 points.

73
00:04:30,330 --> 00:04:33,860
Make the patient a smoker, and a chip
links the change to the lungs.

74
00:04:34,130 --> 00:04:37,040
And when an input barely matters, the app
says so.

75
00:04:40,590 --> 00:04:44,940
The What changed panel lists every edit,
and any of them can be reverted.

76
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:50,680
Now the 3D view, requirement 2.

77
00:04:50,910 --> 00:04:54,140
Rotate, zoom, and hover an artery to see
its probability,

78
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:55,340
threshold and reliability.

79
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:58,180
Click it, and the camera flies there.

80
00:04:58,250 --> 00:05:00,900
The card and the explanation follow the
selection.

81
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:03,710
The left main says plainly: not modelled.

82
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:10,220
There are view presets, a realistic or
clinical look,

83
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:12,440
a gentle heartbeat, and a turntable.

84
00:05:12,490 --> 00:05:15,880
The legend marks each artery's threshold
on the colour scale.

85
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:20,640
Reset, full screen, a screenshot button,
and an automatic quality switch are always

86
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:21,540
at hand.

87
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:28,520
Body mode places the heart in a torso,
with an x-ray slider,

88
00:05:28,570 --> 00:05:31,170
and highlights where contributing factors
live.

89
00:05:31,530 --> 00:05:33,960
Territories show what each artery
typically supplies.

90
00:05:37,410 --> 00:05:41,730
Why is requirement 3b: a SHAP waterfall in
probability points,

91
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:43,990
for CAD and for each artery.

92
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:48,290
The breakdown groups the reasons, and the
table puts each measurement beside its

93
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:50,010
typical range and contribution.

94
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,260
That's 3c.

95
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:57,310
What-if changes only modifiable factors.

96
00:05:57,400 --> 00:06:01,750
Lower LDL, lower blood pressure, stop
smoking, and the table shows before and

97
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:06,670
after. Show on heart previews the colours,
and holding compares with the original.

98
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:10,210
A sensitivity chart sweeps one factor
across its range.

99
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:17,870
The model card is our honesty page:
hold-out metrics with intervals,

100
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,290
validation, thresholds, calibration, and
limitations.

101
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:24,850
It also shows how each sample patient
actually turned out.

102
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:31,420
Export a PDF report, with the disclaimer
on every page,

103
00:06:31,650 --> 00:06:34,300
copy a plain summary, or save a
screenshot.

104
00:06:37,950 --> 00:06:41,620
An optional education card explains risk
factors in general,

105
00:06:41,670 --> 00:06:44,400
with sources, and never changes the heart.

106
00:06:44,450 --> 00:06:45,900
There's a light theme too.

107
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:53,690
It adapts to tablets and phones, and loads
a lighter model automatically on weaker

108
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:54,510
devices.

109
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:02,010
If the server drops, a banner explains it,
the last result stays,

110
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,270
and the app reconnects by itself.

111
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:06,810
And every shortcut is one key away.

112
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:14,340
Under the hood: the frozen ML package
feeds the anatomy layer,

113
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:17,980
a FastAPI service exposes ten endpoints
with one error shape,

114
00:07:18,030 --> 00:07:21,220
and React Three Fiber binds the scene to
the heart.

115
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:24,360
The frontend holds no clinical data of its
own.

116
00:07:24,410 --> 00:07:26,940
A guard script fails the build if it ever
does.

117
00:07:28,890 --> 00:07:32,060
Everything is tested: 49 Python tests, 22
unit tests,

118
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:36,940
and 34 browser tests, including one that
checks every artery's rendered colour

119
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,380
against the API.

120
00:07:38,610 --> 00:07:43,360
Accessibility scans find no serious
issues, the viewer runs near 60 frames per

121
00:07:43,410 --> 00:07:48,360
second, and Lighthouse scores 88 for
performance and 100 for accessibility.

122
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:53,600
It's live on Vercel, at havoc-rho dot
vercel dot app.

123
00:07:53,650 --> 00:07:56,420
It also runs in Docker, from a one-click
Windows launcher,

124
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:58,940
and everything rebuilds from one command.

125
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:03,180
Finally, the limits.

126
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:08,120
This is one hospital's data, 303 patients,
with no external validation and no lesion

127
00:08:08,170 --> 00:08:12,180
location, and the RCA model is only of
limited reliability.

128
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:15,440
CardioLens is for decision support and
education only.

129
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:19,600
It is not a substitute for diagnostic
imaging or clinical judgement.

130
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:23,000
Thanks to the dataset authors, to
neshallads for the heart,

131
00:08:23,050 --> 00:08:24,380
and to Poly Haven.

132
00:08:24,430 --> 00:08:26,160
From Team HAVOC, thank you.
